In Linux, you can easily find the size of a file in kilobytes kb using the ls, du, or stat command.
Linux is an open-source, Unix-like operating system that is widely used for servers, desktops, and embedded systems. It was created by Linus Torvalds in 1991 and is known for its stability, security, and flexibility. Linux is based on the Linux Kernel and supports a variety of distributions like Ubuntu, Fedora, CentOS, and Debian. It is commonly used in web servers, cloud computing, mobile devices, and IoT (Internet of Things). Linux is free to use, modify, and distribute, making it popular among developers, businesses, and system administrators.
